WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.063 --> 00:00:09.808
The witch took off her shawl.

2
00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.401
She spread it on the ground.

3
00:00:12.402 --> 00:00:15.689
Then she pointed at it.

4
00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:20.646
"Get on," she croaked.

5
00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:28.422
Rapunzel sat on the shawl.

6
00:00:28.423 --> 00:00:32.289
"Up!" the witch said.

7
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:36.067
Rapunzel blinked in surprise.

8
00:00:36.068 --> 00:00:42.213
The shawl floated into the air!

9
00:00:42.214 --> 00:00:48.599
The shawl flew above the road.

10
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.522
Soon they reached the city.

11
00:00:53.523 --> 00:01:03.413
Rapunzel saw the market and the king's palace.

12
00:01:03.414 --> 00:01:09.012
At last the shawl landed near a house.

13
00:01:09.013 --> 00:01:15.158
"We're home," the witch said.

14
00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:17.023
Rapunzel scowled.

15
00:01:17.024 --> 00:01:24.440
"This is not my home!" she thought.

16
00:01:24.441 --> 00:01:28.783
Rapunzel followed the witch inside.

17
00:01:28.784 --> 00:01:32.797
There was a room with a bed and desk.

18
00:01:32.798 --> 00:01:42.479
"This is your bedroom," the witch said.

19
00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.050
The witch led her through the rest of the house.

20
00:01:47.051 --> 00:01:50.716
There was a big kitchen.

21
00:01:50.717 --> 00:01:54.446
Another room was a library.

22
00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:59.248
Rapunzel gazed at all the books on magic.

23
00:01:59.249 --> 00:02:03.010
"Can I learn magic?" she asked hopefully.

24
00:02:03.011 --> 00:02:06.873
With the right spells, she could go home and—

25
00:02:06.874 --> 00:02:12.195
"No!" the witch snapped. "Well . . .

26
00:02:12.196 --> 00:02:16.469
Maybe you can help me with healing potions.

27
00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:19.880
But magic can be dangerous.

28
00:02:19.881 --> 00:02:25.586
You must never come into this library alone!"

29
00:02:25.587 --> 00:02:30.946
Rapunzel sighed and followed the witch outside.

30
00:02:30.947 --> 00:02:35.381
They went into a beautiful garden.

31
00:02:35.382 --> 00:02:41.490
"I use these plants for healing potions," the witch said.

32
00:02:41.491 --> 00:02:45.442
"You will take good care of them."

33
00:02:45.443 --> 00:02:51.325
Rapunzel smiled. "I like gardening."

34
00:02:51.326 --> 00:02:54.931
She started weeding.

35
00:02:54.932 --> 00:03:00.602
The witch nodded. "Good girl."

36
00:03:00.603 --> 00:03:06.664
She went back into the house.

37
00:03:06.665 --> 00:03:11.436
Rapunzel took out the hedgehog.

38
00:03:11.437 --> 00:03:15.093
"I will call you Prickle," she whispered.

39
00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:17.799
"You can live in this garden."

40
00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:24.740
Prickle squeaked.

41
00:03:24.741 --> 00:03:37.222
Rapunzel sang as she worked.

42
00:03:37.223 --> 00:03:44.793
The witch returned. "You have a pretty voice."

43
00:03:44.794 --> 00:03:49.756
"I was singing Mama's favorite song," Rapunzel said.

44
00:03:49.757 --> 00:03:56.485
The witch growled. "Forget your parents!

45
00:03:56.486 --> 00:03:59.636
And never sing that song again.

46
00:03:59.637 --> 00:04:13.469
You belong here now—with me!"

